<DocsLayout title="Haft roadmap after v9.0" description="The v9 release boundary, explicitly deferred research, and where to verify future release work without turning candidates into promises.">
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>

  <p>
    v9.0.0 is the current release. This page separates it from later candidates
    and research. A proposal, issue, source branch, or schema is not a product
    commitment.
  </p>

  <h2>Included in v9.0</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>source-native FPF concern query, exact lookup, and exact inspection;</li>
    <li>12 independent host-agent skills;</li>
    <li>fused code and reasoning graph orientation;</li>
    <li>project-profile onboarding and default typed project memory;</li>
    <li>exact EntityOfConcern resolve, neighborhood, and bounded recall;</li>
    <li>typed SpecSection lifecycle and source-currentness repair;</li>
    <li>runner-neutral WorkCommission and RuntimeRun records;</li>
    <li>CLI, skills, and MCP over one project graph.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deliberately outside v9.0</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>a standalone coding agent, TUI, or desktop wrapper;</li>
    <li><code>haft run</code>, <code>haft harness</code>, and bundled Open-Sleigh execution;</li>
    <li>a public <code>h-plan</code> skill or universal reasoning workflow;</li>
    <li>automatic execution, local patch application, merge, push, deploy, or publication authority;</li>
    <li>reviewed EntityOfConcern merge/split as a public v9 identity change;</li>
    <li>any claim that dense or hybrid retrieval outperforms FTS, <code>rg</code>, a pinned FPF file, or host RAG.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    The optional <code>haft-embed</code> sidecar remains a compatibility
    component outside the v9 contract and P14 acceptance basis.
  </p>

  <h2>Deferred work is not release status</h2>

  <p>
    Later v9.x work may revisit the explicitly deferred identity-reconciliation
    and retrieval-evaluation boundaries. Until one exact candidate is
    implemented, qualified, authorized, and released, those remain proposals
    or research rather than current product behavior.
  </p>

  <p>
    The return condition for a stronger claim is the same as for v9.0: current
    evidence tied to one exact candidate, followed by release authorization.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to verify current work</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a> for current release status;</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a> for shipped release history;</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issues</a> for open work and discussion;</li>
    <li><code>haft version</code>, <code>haft doctor</code>, and <code>haft interface</code> for the installed runtime surface.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Runtime inspection proves only the installation being inspected. It does
    not turn an unreleased development binary into the current product.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
